--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STANDALONE VERIFICATION (compensating for the unavailable xcodebuild step)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Because xcodebuild cannot run, the surface was type-checked directly against the
installed macOS 15 SDK with `swiftc -typecheck`, under the project's real build
flags (-swift-version 6 -strict-concurrency=complete), together with the generated
design tokens (apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift).

Toolchain note (artifacts of CLT, not the surface):
  * `@Observable` — the CLT 6.3.2 macro plugin mis-reports its own `shouldNotifyObservers`
    helper ("declaration name 'shouldNotifyObservers' is not covered by macro 'Observable'").
    Reproduced with a 3-line minimal @Observable class, so it is the standalone plugin,
    not this code. The whole TeslaSync app uses @MainActor @Observable, so the real Xcode
    build resolves it. For the standalone check the two macro ATTRIBUTES (@Observable /
    @ObservationIgnored) were stripped from a temp copy; all logic/types are unchanged.
  * `#Preview` (PreviewsMacros) and `XCTest` are Xcode-only. Preview bodies were
    type-checked by rewriting `#Preview {...}` into `@ViewBuilder func -> some View`;
    test bodies were type-checked against the real surface types behind a minimal
    XCTest shim (XCTestCase + XCTAssert*). No surface source was altered.

Results (all against MacOSX15.sdk, arm64-apple-macos15.0, swift 6, strict concurrency):
  swiftc -typecheck  Tokens + HelpTooltip.Model + .Views + .swift ............ EXIT=0
  swiftc -typecheck  + rewritten HelpTooltip.Previews bodies ................. EXIT=0
  swiftc -typecheck  + HelpTooltip.Tests bodies (via XCTest shim) ............ EXIT=0
A real strict-concurrency defect WAS caught and fixed this way: the test-file global
translators are now `@Sendable` (else #MutableGlobalVariable would fail the test build).

RUNTIME LOGIC VERIFICATION (executed, not just type-checked):
A swiftc-built executable (Tokens + HelpTooltip.Model[attrs-stripped] + .Views + a
harness mirroring the XCTest assertions) was COMPILED and RUN against MacOSX15.sdk
under -swift-version 6. All 18 logic assertions passed at runtime (RUN_EXIT=0, "ALL_PASS"):
  literalText, literalVisible, emptyHides, nilHides, i18nTranslated, i18nFallback,
  i18nMissingNoDefaultHidden, defaultIconLabel, ariaOverride, learnMoreDefault,
  learnMoreCustom, learnMoreSuppressedWhenHidden, placementSizeCarried,
  arrowEdgeMapping, pointSizeMapping, telemetryOnce, telemetrySilentWhenHidden, slug.
This exercises the real projection, content-resolution, learn-more, placement/size
mapping, and telemetry-once model logic end-to-end (the XCTest bodies that the
hosted test target will re-run under XCUnit once the surface is wired in).

