IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY (production-polished, no stubs)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/):
  HelpTooltip.swift          generic SwiftUI surface: "?" trigger + popover; default-icon
                             initializer + custom-trigger initializer (web `children`).
  HelpTooltip.Model.swift    P1/S11 telemetry seam (view.opened), P1/S10 i18n facade,
                             config/placement/size/learn-more value types, pure
                             HelpTooltipProjection (the testable adapter), @MainActor
                             @Observable HelpTooltipModel (telemetry-once).
  HelpTooltip.Views.swift    default "?" glyph, popover bubble (text + learn-more Link),
                             placement->arrowEdge & size->pointSize mappings.
  HelpTooltip.Previews.swift 7 #Previews: default / learn-more / placements / sizes /
                             custom trigger / hidden(empty).
  HelpTooltip.Tests.swift    projection, label/learn-more, placement+size mapping,
                             telemetry-once, per-variant ImageRenderer render smoke,
                             resolved a11y label, hidden invariant.
  HelpTooltip.strings        P1/S10 catalog contribution.

Parity with components/ui/HelpTooltip.tsx:
  * props text / i18nKey / defaultValue / placement / learnMore / size / ariaLabel /
    children  -> all reproduced (children = custom-trigger initializer).
  * content resolution  i18nKey ? t(i18nKey,{defaultValue}) : (text ?? '')  -> projection.
  * `if (!resolved) return null`  -> surface renders nothing when content is empty.
  * shared <Tooltip> (hover/focus/tap, ARIA, placement, reduced-motion)  -> native
    .popover + .help() + system focus/dismiss; `side` -> arrowEdge; multiline max-w-260
    -> .frame(maxWidth: 260).
  * learn-more <a target="_blank"> + external-link glyph  -> SwiftUI Link + arrow.up.right.

States: the web source's only branches are content-present (visible) and empty
(hidden / `return null`); both render. The generic loading/error/stale/offline axes
are N/A for this leaf — its sole data source is `useTranslation` (no fetch), so there
is no loadable state. Documented in-source, not faked (Honesty Covenant #2/#9).

i18n keys (all via the P1/S10 facade; no English literals in Swift):
  help.tooltip.iconLabel = "More info"   |   common.learnMore = "Learn more"
  helpTooltip.learnMoreHint = "Opens in your browser" (native a11y hint for the link)

Telemetry: HelpTooltipModel.onAppear emits view.opened with slug "HelpTooltip" once,
suppressed when the surface is hidden (P1/S11).

Accessibility: trigger has an explicit VoiceOver label (iconLabel, ariaLabel-overridable);
glyphs are accessibilityHidden; learn-more Link carries label + hint; text uses
.fixedSize(vertical) so it wraps under Dynamic Type; popover transitions are system-driven
(reduce-motion respected by the platform).

